% A constructor-arity error suppresses its own unit's warning.
%
% Arity errors are found without the solver, so the two halves of the
% checker have to number their checking units the same way: `dead` is
% both dead (contradicting evidence at a `color`-typed position) and
% wrong (`red/1` at a nullary constructor), and only the error is
% reported. If the arity error landed in a different unit than the
% rule's own diagnostics, the warning would survive.
:- module(typecheck_suppression_arity_unit, []).
:- use_module(library(prelude)).

:- chr_type color ---> red ; green ; blue.
:- chr_constraint tag(color, int), sink(any).

dead @ tag(X, R) <=> integer(X) | R = 1, sink(red(1)).
